  "headline": "Sulfamethoxazole and trimethoprim is not on FDA's shortage list as of 2026-10-21; current inventory shows 26.9 days at Corvale East and 29.5 days at Corvale General",
  "headline_cites": ["D3", "D1", "D2"],
  "sentences": [
    {
      "text": "FDA's drug shortage list does not include sulfamethoxazole and trimethoprim as of 2026-10-21.",
      "cites": ["D3"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Corvale East holds 401 tablets of the 800 mg + 160 mg presentation with 14.9 tablets used per day, providing 26.9 days on hand.",
      "cites": ["D1"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Corvale General holds 469 tablets of the same presentation with 15.9 tablets used per day, providing 29.5 days on hand.",
      "cites": ["D2"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The product label identifies NuCare Pharmaceuticals, Inc. as the labeler and a registered repack plant (FEI 3003294404) last inspected with NAI classification on 2025-03-12.",
      "cites": ["E9"]
    },
    {
      "text": "FDA inspection records for that plant show multiple VAI classifications from 2010 through 2020 and a Warning Letter issued on 2019-09-27.",
      "cites": ["E3", "E4", "E5", "E7", "E8"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The rule-based alternate manufacturer ranked first is Amneal Pharmaceuticals LLC, whose plant Amneal Pharmaceuticals Private Limited received an NAI classification on 2024-07-19.",
      "cites": ["D4"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Buyer should verify current allocation status with Amneal Pharmaceuticals LLC and monitor the NuCare plant's inspection history for any future regulatory actions.",
      "cites": ["D4", "E9"]
    }
  ]
}
